JGraphicEngine License 1.0 (JGEL-1.0)
Short Name: JEngine License (JEL)
Copyright © 2025 JesseTheCatLover
Applies to: JGraphicEngine, also known as “JEngine”

1. Permission and Open-Source Grant
This software (“JGraphicEngine”, also referred to as “JEngine”) is provided free of charge.
Permission is granted to any person obtaining a copy of the Software to:
- use the Software for any purpose, commercial or non-commercial;
- modify the Software;
- create derivative works (“forks”);
- distribute original or modified copies of the Software.
No fees, royalties, or prior approval are required.

2. Attribution Requirement
Redistributions, forks, or derivative works must preserve attribution to the original project and its author.
Attribution may be expressed in any reasonable form, including but not limited to documentation, credits, metadata, or source headers, so long as it clearly acknowledges that JGraphicEngine (JEngine) and its original implementation were created by JesseTheCatLover.
Attribution must not be removed, concealed, falsified, or minimized in a misleading way.

3. Naming and Identity Integrity
3.1 Protected Names
The official names of this software are:
- JGraphicEngine (formal and historical name)
- JEngine (short and public name)

3.2 Fork Naming Rules
Forks must not fully rename the engine or remove its identity.
A fork must continue to identify itself as a version of JEngine, but may add its own identifier or branding.
Examples of permitted names:
- NeoJEngine
- MyStudio’s JEngine Build
- JEngine — Custom Edition by XYZ
Examples of prohibited names:
- NewEngine (removes identity)
- JEngine Official (implies false authority)
- ForkEngine or any name removing JEngine identity completely

3.3 Identity Accuracy
Forks must not present themselves as:
- the official JEngine project,
- endorsed by the original author,
- replacements for the canonical version.
They must accurately state their relationship as forks or modified versions.

4. Trademark & Logo Usage
The following are protected trademarks of JesseTheCatLover:
- the names “JGraphicEngine” and “JEngine”,
- the stylized “J” logo,
- any official graphical branding or derivative identity marks.

Allowed:
You may use the protected names and logo when giving attribution, linking to the project, or factually describing its usage.

Not Allowed:
You may not:
- use the stylized J logo as your fork’s branding,
- use the protected names in a way that implies official status,
- use the marks in a deceptive or misleading manner.
Trademark rights survive regardless of modifications to the code.

5. License Inheritance (Upstream License Preservation)
Any redistributed or modified version of this Software must include this license in full.
Forks may add additional restrictions or supplemental terms, but no clause of this license may be removed, weakened, or altered.
This ensures preservation of origin, identity, naming, attribution, and trademark rules in all downstream versions.

6. Patent Grant
Contributors and users grant a perpetual, worldwide, royalty-free patent license covering any contributions or modifications they submit to the Software.

7. Warranty Disclaimer
The Software is provided “AS IS”, without warranty of any kind, express or implied, including but not limited to:
- merchantability,
- fitness for a particular purpose,
- non-infringement.
In no event shall the author or any contributor be liable for any damages arising from the use of the Software.

8. Alias Definition and Historical Preservation
“JEngine” is the canonical public name used for branding, documentation, and splash screens.
“JGraphicEngine” is the formal and historical name of the project.
Both names refer to the same software and must be preserved in attribution and lineage.
Forks must maintain the historical chain:
“Forked from JGraphicEngine (JEngine).”

9. Termination Clause
Rights granted under this license terminate automatically if the user:
- removes or falsifies attribution,
- violates naming or identity rules,
- misuses trademarks or logos,
- presents a fork as the official JEngine,
- removes this license from redistributed versions.
Rights may be reinstated upon correction of the violation.

